;; AN ILLUSTRATIVE SCENARIO. NOT A MEASUREMENT OF ANY REAL FLOOD.
;;
;; Every number below was chosen by the author to be internally consistent and
;; to make the model's couplings visible. None of them is observed. They exist
;; so that the structure can be exercised and its behaviour argued about --
;; which is a different activity from estimating what a particular town will
;; need, and mebuki.needs stamps every result produced from this file so the
;; two cannot be confused downstream.
;;
;; If you want an estimate for a real event, bind a jurisdiction profile with
;; measured parameters. If a parameter is not measured, the honest output is
;; that it is not measured.
{:profile/id :scenario/illustrative-medium-town
 :profile/kind :scenario
 :scenario/illustrative true
 :profile/label {:ja "例示シナリオ：中規模の町（実測ではない）"
                 :en "Illustrative scenario: a medium-sized town (not measured)"}
 :scenario/sketch
 "A town where roughly three thousand buildings took water above floor level in
  one night, the river fell within three days, and the response phase has ended.
  Temperate climate, timber-frame housing with plasterboard, a functioning
  rental market, an organised volunteer centre, and a waste site found in the
  first week."
